; tests/dense-family-band.fk — does ONE Form cell carry the dense family, geometry all the file's?
;
; PROOF LEVEL: FOURTH-ARM ONLY. Every bit needs a live Metal device behind the handle door. Bit 1
; is the canary; without it the fold answers 0, which is a REFUSAL, not a verdict, and a skip is
; not a pass either.
;
; Verdict 1023 = 1+2+4+8+16+32+64+128+256+512, POWER-OF-TWO WEIGHTS so a reader can subtract.
;
;   bit    1  THE DOOR IS REAL. metal_linked=true AND metal_door=handle, asked of the one
;             primitive that speaks, before anything below is believed.
;   bit    2  THE FILE IS THE ONE PINNED, AND TWO INDEPENDENT WALKS AGREE. The GGUF magic at
;             absolute offset 0 and the tensor count 147 at absolute offset 8 are read with eqr-at
;             at HAND-PINNED offsets (independent anchors — not through the table walk the loop
;             uses). Then the METADATA's geometry is checked against the TENSOR TABLE's own dims:
;             attn_q rows = head_count * head_dim, attn_k rows = kv head count * head_dim,
;             ffn_gate rows = feed_forward_length, unembedding rows = vocab. Two walks of two
;             different header regions must agree — a co-moved reference cannot fail; two
;             independent ones can.
;   bit    4  EVERY KERNEL COMPILED — all 45 pipelines answer nonzero (2026-08-08 round two
;             added the six factored-scale lane2 matvecs, the tiled and wide RMSNorms, the
;             three attention maps and the neox pair rope). A zero is an MSL diagnostic held
;             in metal_status.
;   bit    8  THE WEIGHTS ARE RESIDENT, NOT COPIED: mmap_nocopy_buffers=148 for this file (147
;             tensors + the tied unembedding's second view).
;   bit   16  THE BODY'S TOKENIZER AGREES WITH THE RECORDED ANCHOR. dtk-encode of "The capital
;             of France is" = [128000 791 6864 315 9822 374] — the ids committed in
;             llama-token-handle-band.fk (2e914252e), produced there by the retired harness's
;             encoder, reproduced here by the body's own longest-match. An anchor RECORDED
;             BEFORE this cell existed, not recomputed through it.
;   bit   32  ONE TOKEN. First generated id 12366, witnessed 2026-08-04 by dense-run-llama1b.fk
;             and pinned here. Same input, same id, every run — greedy is a rule.
;   bit   64  THE STREAM, ALL 16: 12366 13 578 469 3168 301 22703 374 7559 304 12366 13 578 9928
;             49606 16730 — sixteen positions of KV-cache reuse, witnessed 2026-08-04.
;   bit  128  THE BODY READS ITS OWN ANSWER: the sixteen ids through l3d-text spell
;             " Paris. The Eiffel Tower is located in Paris. The Louvre Museum".
;   bit  256  THE LOOP NEVER WAITS: total_dispatch=6489 and total_sync=21 — 21 forwards, 309
;             dispatches each, ONE sync per forward, read from the carrier's counters.
;             (2026-08-04 the count was 276/forward at 5796; 2026-08-08 the two-stage argmax
;             made the head five dispatches instead of four, moving it to 277 at 5817; later
;             the same day round two split attention into three bit-exact dispatches —
;             scores/soft/out — so a layer is 19 and a forward is 16 x 19 + 5 = 309. The gate
;             moved WITH the recipe each time; the 2026-08-08 sweep witnessed the identical
;             two-prompt streams at both counts.)
;   bit  512  A SECOND ARCH THROUGH THE SAME CELL. MiniCPM5-1B: prompt ids [608 4894 304 6918
;             357] (its file says add_bos=0 and the cell obeys the file), first id 8181 —
;             witnessed 2026-08-04. This is the path where head_dim comes from key_length (128,
;             NOT d/nHead=96), the unembedding is untied, and rope_freqs does not exist so the
;             cell writes ones.
;
; WHAT THIS BAND CANNOT SEE: speed; the qwen2/nanbeige/phi2 paths (witnessed by their run
; drivers, recorded in receipts/2026-08-04-dense-family-form-loop.md); sampling other than
; greedy; sequences past maxpos 256.
;
; MUTATION TABLE — predictions WRITTEN BEFORE RUNNING, then reconciled. A falsifier through a
; raw-constant door needs a CLOCK as well as a verdict (row 987 stallred), so every mutation run
; is wrapped in a 300 s timeout by the runner.
;
;   clean                                              predict 1023  ACTUAL 1023  agreed
;   M-1  dth-price returns 0 for Q8_0 (type 8)         predict 23    ACTUAL 23    agreed
;        (1+2+4+16: views refuse, residency count moves, tokenizer needs no weights)
;   M-2  this band's llama open forced to neox rope    predict 799   ACTUAL 831   DISAGREED
;        Predicted 1023-32-64-128; bit 32 HELD. The first token after "The capital of France is"
;        is so strongly determined that the argmax SURVIVES a wrong rope pair layout across six
;        prefill positions; only the sixteen-token stream (64) and its text (128) fell. A
;        one-token gate is blind to rope style. The stream is the witness; the single id is not.
;   M-3  the V-cache copy dropped from dth-block       predict 31    ACTUAL 31    agreed
;        (1+2+4+8+16: dispatch count moves so 256 falls, both models' ids turn)
;   M-4  dth-bool's absent-default flipped to 0        predict 783   ACTUAL 559   DISAGREED
;        twice, in opposite directions. Bit 32 HELD again — " Paris" survives a missing BOS too.
;        And bit 256 FELL: the prediction said "21 forwards of 276 is still 5796/21", but a
;        missing BOS is a missing FORWARD — 5 prompt ids + 15 = 20 forwards, 5520/20. The count
;        gate saw the fault the prediction reasoned away; the arithmetic in the prediction was
;        wrong, and the reconciliation is the record of it. MiniCPM5 (512) was immune as
;        predicted: its file declares add_bos=0 and never consults the default.
;
;   The two disagreements agree with each other: the single-token bit survived BOTH faults it
;   was predicted to catch. What proves this stack is the STREAM — sixteen mutually-consistent
;   picks — never one strongly-determined token. (Row 988 proposal, proseproof.)
;
; preludes: native/metal/dense-token-handle.fk
;
; witnessed: 2026-08-04, fkwu-metal (fourth arm), Apple M4 Max

(do
    (defn dfb-blob () "/Users/ursmuff/.ollama/models/blobs/sha256-74701a8c35f6c8d9a4b91f3f3497643001d63e0c7a84e085bed452548fa88d45")
    (defn dfb-blob2 () "/Users/ursmuff/.ollama/models/blobs/sha256-0dc7638539067268774c275a14a6ec9c7e01f7eeb2cff606c8590361fa527e4c")
    (defn dfb-prompt () "The capital of France is")
    (defn dfb-want-prompt () (list 128000 791 6864 315 9822 374))
    (defn dfb-want () (list 12366 13 578 469 3168 301 22703 374 7559 304 12366 13 578 9928 49606 16730))
    (defn dfb-want-text () " Paris. The Eiffel Tower is located in Paris. The Louvre Museum")
    (defn dfb-want-prompt2 () (list 608 4894 304 6918 357))

    (defn dfb-eqlist (a b)
        (if (eq (len a) (len b))
            (if (eq (len a) 0) true
                (if (eq (head a) (head b)) (dfb-eqlist (tail a) (tail b)) false))
            false))

    (let live (md-door-live?))

    ; ---- bit 2's independent anchors: bytes at hand-pinned absolute offsets ----
    (let src0 (dth-src (dfb-blob)))
    (let magic-ok (if (eq (eqr-at src0 0) 71)          ; 'G'
                  (if (eq (eqr-at src0 1) 71)          ; 'G'
                  (if (eq (eqr-at src0 2) 85)          ; 'U'
                      (eq (eqr-at src0 3) 70) false) false) false))  ; 'F'
    (let tcount-ok (eq (egg-u64 src0 8) 147))

    ; ---- open, and the two-walk agreement ----
    (let st (dth-open (dfb-blob) 256 (sub 0 1)))
    (let ps (nth st 0)) (let bs (nth st 1)) (let geo (nth st 2))
    (let lays (nth st 3)) (let cks (nth st 4)) (let cvs (nth st 5))
    (let embTv (nth st 6)) (let onormTv (nth st 7)) (let projTv (nth st 8))
    (let src (nth st 10))

    (let l0 (nth lays 0))
    (let dims-agree (if (eq (dth-tv-r (nth l0 1)) (nth geo 13))        ; attn_q rows = qOut
                    (if (eq (dth-tv-r (nth l0 2)) (nth geo 5))         ; attn_k rows = kvd
                    (if (eq (dth-tv-r (nth l0 6)) (nth geo 1))         ; ffn_gate rows = dFF
                        (eq (dth-tv-r projTv) (nth geo 7)) false) false) false))
    (let geo-ok (if magic-ok (if tcount-ok dims-agree false) false))

    (let pipes-ok (dth-pipe-ok? ps))

    (let ids (dtk-encode src (dfb-prompt)))
    (let tok-ok (dfb-eqlist ids (dfb-want-prompt)))

    (let resident (md-status-has? "mmap_nocopy_buffers=148"))

    (let pf (dth-prefill ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv ids 0))
    (let first (nth pf 0))
    (let rest (dth-generate ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv first (len ids) 15 (empty)))
    (let got (append (list first) rest))
    (let text (l3d-text src got))
    (let shape-ok (if (md-status-has? "total_dispatch=6489") (md-status-has? "total_sync=21") false))

    ; ---- the second arch, same cell ----
    (let st2 (dth-open (dfb-blob2) 256 (sub 0 1)))
    (let ids2 (dtk-encode (nth st2 10) (dfb-prompt)))
    (let pf2 (dth-prefill (nth st2 0) (nth st2 1) (nth st2 2) (nth st2 3) (nth st2 4) (nth st2 5)
                          (nth st2 6) (nth st2 7) (nth st2 8) ids2 0))
    (let arch2-ok (if (dfb-eqlist ids2 (dfb-want-prompt2)) (eq (nth pf2 0) 8181) false))

    (add (if live 1 0)
    (add (if live (if geo-ok 2 0) 0)
    (add (if live (if pipes-ok 4 0) 0)
    (add (if live (if resident 8 0) 0)
    (add (if live (if tok-ok 16 0) 0)
    (add (if live (if (eq first 12366) 32 0) 0)
    (add (if live (if (dfb-eqlist got (dfb-want)) 64 0) 0)
    (add (if live (if (str_eq text (dfb-want-text)) 128 0) 0)
    (add (if live (if shape-ok 256 0) 0)
         (if live (if arch2-ok 512 0) 0)))))))))))
